EXAMPLES=[{'num':'2','title':'Two False-Position Iterations','question':'Perform two regula-falsi iterations for sin x−e^(−x)=0 on [0.5,0.7], with x in radians.','steps':['f is continuous, f(0.5)≈−0.12710512, f(0.7)≈0.14763238. Keep a=0.5,b=0.7.','Use the chord formula c=a−(a−b)f(a)/(f(a)−f(b)).','First iterate c₀≈0.5925284091; f(c₀)≈0.0055327114>0. Keep [0.5,0.5925284091].','Reapply the formula with those new endpoints and their unrounded function values.','Second iterate c₁≈0.5886687790; f(c₁)≈0.0001886563>0. Keep [0.5,0.5886687790].','Both chord intersections are inside their current brackets. The source residual 0.081 at its first point is wrong, and its denominator sign yields an invalid 0.755 outside the bracket.','The final approximation is 0.5886687790 after two steps. Its residual is small, but the remaining bracket width is still about 0.0886687790; do not confuse residual with a general guaranteed root-error bound.'],'answer':'c₀≈0.5925284091; c₁≈0.5886687790; final bracket [0.5,0.5886687790].','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':313,'jpg':'161_page_1.jpg','verification':'Printed calculations visually checked and correct two iterations independently computed'}]}]
